   "type": "User",
   "user_view_type": "public",
   "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "If a worker was asked to start a task it was already running, it threw\nan error and the task was marked as FAILED, even though the original\ntask was still running fine. The worker now logs a warning and skips\nthe duplicate start, so the running task keeps its status.\n\nConnectors were not affected: a duplicate connector start already only\nlogs an error and does not change the connector's status.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
